                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "28432791",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561197970882842",
                            "num_reviews": 30,
                            "playtime_forever": 170,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 147,
                            "last_played": 1497790828
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I haven't played a whole lot of VR games yet but this is one of my favorites so far.  It's a curious mix of a deck management card game with a wave shooter, I suppose.  You kill mobs before your foe can in order to earn points to spend on the use of one of five or so cards you've drawn from your deck which might help you or hurt your foe.  I didn't really know what to expect when buying it, but the result really tickles my fancy.\n\nIt's challenge is in the mix of accurately shooting, managing your points, choosing your attack cards at the right time, and saving points for defensive cards to thwart your enemy's attacks.  \n\nIt suffers from a lack of explanation as to these mechanics, but you'll learn fast playing in single player.  The early bot is easy to beat once you get used to the mechanics, then once you hit level 6 or so, the bot gets a lot harder to challenge you.  I wish they let you choose the difficulty of the bot, though, as my friends can't beat the harder bot without the experience of the easier one first.\n\nIt could also use a lot more players in MP right now.  I've had the most luck playing against Chinese players late at night, which are pretty plentiful.\n\nI see a lot of room for future expansion in this game, with new cards, new kaijus and new weapons to choose from.  I hope this game has a bright future.",
